body:
Received TRUNCATE request references Index table - 't3_k_idx' id=*4303, instead of the main table 't3' id=*4300:
```
I1202 14:59:52.982560 21200 catalog_manager.cc:2589] Servicing TruncateTable request from 127.0.0.1:42229: table_ids: "000030a9000030008000000000004303"
I1202 14:59:52.982586 21200 catalog_manager.cc:2617] TABLE PB: name: "t3_k_idx" version: 0 schema { columns { id: 10 name: "k" type { main: INT32 } is_key: true is_hash_key: true is_nullable: false is_static: false is_counter: false sorting_type: 0 order: 1 } columns { id: 11 name: "ybidxbasectid" type { main: BINARY } is_key: true is_nullable: false is_static: false is_counter: false sorting_type: 1 order: -101 } table_properties { contain_counters: false is_transactional: true consistency_level: STRONG use_mangled_column_name: false } } state: RUNNING next_column_id: 12 partition_schema { range_schema { } hash_schema: PGSQL_HASH_SCHEMA } table_type: PGSQL_TABLE_TYPE namespace_id: "000030a9000030008000000000000000" indexed_table_id: "000030a9000030008000000000004300" is_local_index: false is_unique_index: false index_info { table_id: "000030a9000030008000000000004303" indexed_table_id: "000030a9000030008000000000004300" }
```
But in the source code expected only BASE table, not an index:
```
Status CatalogManager::TruncateTable(const TruncateTableRequestPB* req,
                                     TruncateTableResponsePB* resp,
                                     rpc::RpcContext* rpc) {
  LOG(INFO) << "Servicing TruncateTable request from " << RequestorString(rpc)
            << ": " << req->ShortDebugString();

  RETURN_NOT_OK(CheckOnline());

  for (int i = 0; i < req->table_ids_size(); i++) {
    RETURN_NOT_OK(TruncateTable(req->table_ids(i), false /* is_index */, resp, rpc));
<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< is_index == FALSE always
  }
```

In fact the Postgres side truncate the main table and the indexes after that:
```
void
YBCTruncateTable(Relation rel) {
	YBCPgStatement handle;
	Oid relationId = RelationGetRelid(rel);

	/* Truncate the base table */
	HandleYBStatus(YBCPgNewTruncateTable(ybc_pg_session, MyDatabaseId, relationId, &handle));
	HandleYBStmtStatus(YBCPgExecTruncateTable(handle), handle);
	HandleYBStatus(YBCPgDeleteStatement(handle));

	if (!rel->rd_rel->relhasindex)
		return;

	/* Truncate the associated secondary indexes */
	List	 *indexlist = RelationGetIndexList(rel);
	ListCell *lc;

	foreach(lc, indexlist)
	{
		Oid indexId = lfirst_oid(lc);

		if (indexId == rel->rd_pkindex)
			continue;

		HandleYBStatus(YBCPgNewTruncateTable(ybc_pg_session, MyDatabaseId, indexId, &handle));
		HandleYBStmtStatus(YBCPgExecTruncateTable(handle), handle);
		HandleYBStatus(YBCPgDeleteStatement(handle));
	}

	list_free(indexlist);
}
```
But YB side should automatically delete related indexes if the table was truncated.
So, there are 2 options for the fix:
1) Let's truncate the index, even if it was truncated together with the table.
2) Do not truncate indexes (from Postgres code). (It must be automatically truncated by YB server before - via the TRUNCATE \<table\> request).

The option (2) above is not applicable.
The CatalogManager::TruncateTable automatically truncates associated indexes, but PG table does not have the links in the table record, so the code does nothing for PG table (it truncates indexes for CQL table only at the moment):
```
for (const auto& index_info : l->data().pb.indexes()) {
  RETURN_NOT_OK(TruncateTable(index_info.table_id(), resp, rpc));
```
The links are NOT created for PG table in the CatalogManager::CreateTable():
```
// For index table, insert index info in the indexed table.
if ((req.has_index_info() || req.has_indexed_table_id()) && !is_pg_table) {     <<<<<<<<<<<< !is_pg_table
  s = AddIndexInfoToTable(indexed_table, index_info);
```

issue.body:
Truncating an index crashes yb-master in debug mode.

To replicate:
```
CREATE TABLE ITABLE ( ptest1 int, ptest2 int, ptest3 text);
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ITABLE_IDX ON ITABLE(ptest1, ptest2);
TRUNCATE ITABLE CASCADE;
```

fails with this fatal:
```F1018 19:54:56.574093 12686 catalog_manager.cc:2591] Check failed: is_index == (l->data().pb.has_index_info() || !l->data().pb.indexed_table_id().empty()) ```
